
# Expense Tracker

## Project Description

I created a simple Expense Tracker web page using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. I used ChatGPT as an AI tool to help me build the application.

The purpose of this project is to help users keep track of their daily expenses.

## Features

The Expense Tracker allows users to:

- Add an expense with a name.
- Enter the amount spent.
- Select a category such as Food, Travel, or Shopping.
- View all expenses.
- See the total amount spent.
- Delete an expense.
- See an error message when the name is empty or the amount is zero or negative.

## How I Used AI to Complete the Project

I used ChatGPT to help me understand and build the Expense Tracker.

First, I wrote a prompt explaining what I wanted the application to do.

I used the seven parts of a good prompt:

1. Role - I asked AI to act as a web developer.
2. Context - I explained that I was a beginner working on a class assignment.
3. Task - I asked AI to create an Expense Tracker.
4. Constraints - I asked it to use only HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
5. Examples - I gave an example of adding a Food expense for $25.
6. Output Format - I asked AI to provide the code in separate files.
7. Success Criteria - I explained that the application must add, display, total, and delete expenses.

## How I Built the Application

I used AI to break the project into smaller steps.

First, I created the HTML file to build the webpage.

Next, I used CSS to make the webpage look clean and organized.

Then, I used JavaScript to make the application work. JavaScript allows users to add expenses, delete expenses, and calculate the total amount spent.

I also asked AI to add error messages when users enter incorrect information.

## How I Improved the Application

After creating the application, I asked ChatGPT to review the code and suggest an improvement.

I asked AI to show a message when there are no expenses in the list.

I also reviewed the code and asked AI to explain parts I did not understand.

## Testing the Application

I tested the application using different examples:

- Added groceries for $25.
- Added gas for $40.
- Checked that the total was $65.
- Deleted an expense.
- Tried submitting an empty name.
- Tried entering zero as the amount.
- Tried entering a negative amount.

The application should accept valid expenses and display error messages for invalid information.

## What I Learned

I learned how to use ChatGPT to help create a simple web application.

I learned how to write clear AI prompts, break a project into smaller steps, and review code created by AI.

I also learned how HTML, CSS, and JavaScript work together.

Finally, I learned how to use Git and GitHub to save and manage my project files.

## Technologies Used

- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- ChatGPT AI
- Git
- GitHub

## Conclusion

This project helped me understand how AI can make coding easier for beginners. I learned that AI can help write code, explain problems, and suggest improvements, but it is important to review and test the code to make sure everything works correctly.
